;; `cli` and `test` are deliberately NOT in :paths.
;;
;; Every path listed at the top level lands on the classpath of anything
;; that resolves this port, so :paths is the library and nothing else. The
;; CLI is an example program and the conformance suite is this port's own
;; test; neither is part of what a consumer takes, and the aliases below add
;; them back for the Makefile.
;;
;; :deps is empty for the same reason it is empty in every other port: the
;; library depends on nothing but its language's own runtime, which for
;; Clojure the CLI tool supplies. There is no JSON library here, and no HTTP
;; client - see src/voxgig/sekreto/json.clj and the java.net.http interop in
;; src/voxgig/sekreto/providers.clj.
;;
;; The conformance runner is a checkout, not a published artifact, so it is
;; not named here either: the Makefile puts its source directory on the
;; classpath with -Sdeps, the way the other JVM ports pass a path to their
;; compiler. Nothing a consumer resolves can reach it.
{:paths ["src"]
 :deps {}
 :aliases
 {;; The CLI, and the directory its AOT-compiled classes are written to:
  ;; Clojure's compiler requires *compile-path* to be on the classpath.
  :cli {:extra-paths ["cli" "build/classes"]}

  :test {:extra-paths ["test"]}}}
